  "answers": {
    "vision": {
      "answer": "Most countries follow a positive trend: higher income is associated with longer life expectancy. Notable deviations include **Cuba, Sri Lanka, Jordan, and Costa Rica**, which have relatively high life expectancy for their income levels, while **South Africa, Botswana, Russia, Saudi Arabia, and the United States** have lower life expectancy than similarly wealthy countries.",
